Theory

Page Rank is used to measure importance of nodes in a network.
It was originally used by Google to rank web pages.

In social media, Page Rank can identify:

important users
important pages
influential nodes

It works on graph structure using links between nodes.

Code Explanation
Graph dataset is created/read.
Nodes and edges are formed.
Page Rank algorithm is applied.
Rank score of each node is calculated.
Graph is visualized.
Output
Rank score of nodes
Graph visualization
Conclusion

Thus, Page Rank helps identify important and influential nodes in a social network.
